::SQL Left-and-Right Join::
What is the primary purpose of a LEFT JOIN in SQL?
{
    ~To include only matching records from both tables
    =To include all records from the left table and matching records from the right table
    ~To include all records from the right table and matching records from the left table
    ~To exclude records that have no matching values in the other table
}

::SQL Left-and-Right Join::
What happens if there are no matching records in the right table for a row in the left table in a LEFT JOIN?
{
    ~The row is excluded from the result set
    ~The row is included in the result set with default values for columns from the right table
    =The row is included in the result set with NULL values for columns from the right table
    ~The row is included in the result set with values from the left table only
}

::SQL Left-and-Right Join::
Which of the following statements about RIGHT JOIN is true?
{
    ~ It includes only matching records from both tables.
    = It includes all records from the right table and matching records from the left table.
    ~ It includes all records from the left table and matching records from the right table.
    ~ It excludes records that have no matching values in the other table.
}


